    },
    {
      "text": "with the V1 protocol, the reference implementation, if you had input required on multiple even though you can see that there's many of them in flight, on the client side they were FIFO. So, you could only respond to the first one.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1226,
      "why": "Reports a concrete limitation found in the reference implementation, not just the spec."
    },
    {
      "text": "even though this is better, it still doesn't scale to the millions. Why? Because if I've got a million tasks running, I've got a million clients that are doing gets against each and every one of those tasks. That does not scale.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1311,
      "why": "The main open problem she leaves the audience with."
    },
    {
      "text": "My goal is to actually implement it in in fast MCP so that you can use the same protocol the same framework that you're using probably for your MCP servers today.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1376,
      "why": "States her concrete roadmap commitment with a timeframe."
    }
